scatter "Pickup_Landmark_Clay 1" 2 at -4 -52 r=25 seed=13483 free=2
scatter "Pickup_Landmark_Rock 1" 2 at -4 -52 r=21 seed=13484 free=2
place VP_Excavator hk_dragline at -6.19 -18.59 ground sit yaw=94.4
prop hk_dragline tint.color=#6a5a48
prop hk_dragline tint.amount=0.4
call hw_sunkhouse x=70 z=-22 h=-16 yaw=0 a=hk_sunk chest=hk_deepchest air=hk_air bub=hk_airbub dal=hk_sunkdoor
call hw_zone x=70 z=-22 al=hk_deepz id=hk_deep r=7 h=1 msg="The Union strongroom, 16 metres down. The front room still holds a pocket of air."
place RT_PlasticBoat hk_sunkboat at 78 -20 ground sit yaw=35
prop hk_sunkboat tint.color=#5a5048
prop hk_sunkboat tint.amount=0.45
place Loot_Crate hk_boatcrate at 77 -26 ground sit yaw=10
prop hk_boatcrate loot.refill=0
call hw_reef x=63 z=-17 r=3 seed=13486
place Creature_PufferFish hk_puffers at 64 -29 h=-12
prop hk_puffers creature.count=2
call hw_note x=33.63 z=-19.11 yaw=-108.29 al=hk_hint
story hk_top|Strongroom key|Bolt|Bram Hask's key to the old Union strongroom, hung on a nail at the top of the dragline's boom ladder.
story hk_deep|Bram's tonnage ledger|Note_Paper|Ten years of Council barges, every ton written down - and every one going to the Foundation Piles.
story tape|Insulating tape|Bolt|A roll of the Union linesmen's insulating tape. Three of them would make a dead breaker safe.
note hk_hint Bram's tonnage note | Nailed to the post where the old crane console stood, before the Council took its fuses -\n\nStranger. Teo's runner says you can swim and you can keep your mouth shut. Good. I need both.\n\nThirty years I've written down every ton this yard lifts. Ten years ago I started writing down every ton the Council's barges carry away from it, too. They don't like that. So the ledger lives in the old strongroom, sixteen metres down off the east yard, where no clerk will ever go to fetch it.\n\nThe key's at the top of the dragline's boom ladder on Scrapjaw Heights. I hung it there when my knees still worked. If you've got it, go down and bring the ledger up. Read the last page. Then tell me I'm a mad old man, because I would very much like to be one.\n\n- Bram Hask, foreman
prop hk_deepchest on.open=message||Bram's tonnage ledger, in oilcloth. Ten years of Council barges, every line the same: SCRAP AND STONE TO THE FOUNDATION PILES, BY ORDER, A.C. Eleven thousand tons. Not one barge ever came back loaded.
note hk_topchest Dragline's boom ladder deck box | A box lashed to the deck rail at the top of the dragline's boom ladder.
loot hk_topchest story:hk_top*1;Scrap*3;Bolt*2
note hk_deepchest Union strongroom strongbox | A strongbox in the back room of the Union strongroom.
loot hk_deepchest story:hk_deep*1;story:tape*1;MetalIngot*2
note hk_ledge Climber's cache | A climber's cache on a ledge off the trail - rope, a flask, a few bolts.
loot hk_ledge Rope*2;Bolt*2;Scrap*2
prop hk_ledge loot.refill=0
loot hk_boatcrate Plastic*3;Scrap*2;MetalIngot*1

# --- Settings, story items, notes, behaviours, quests -----------------------------------------------------------------
info title=Hookline Stack
info author=Custom Islands
info description=The Salvagers' Union's yard on a half-sunk office block: three cranes, a zipline between them, scrap piles and ore, a barge of clay and sand, and a dive rope into the drowned street. The fourth island of The City That Never Sank.
island on.arrive=message||Three cranes stand over a yard of scrap. On the half-sunk office block a banner: SALVAGERS' UNION - WHAT WE BRING UP, WE SHARE.

story salvagetag|Salvage tag|Bolt|A diver's brass salvage tag, stamped with the Union's hook - off the drowned street.

prop office tint.color=#8c8a84
prop office tint.amount=0.3
prop skyline tint.color=#7a8088
prop skyline tint.amount=0.4

prop crane1zip obj.name=crane1zip
prop receipt obj.name=receipt
prop receipt beh.hidden=1
prop tag1 obj.name=tag1
prop tag1 beh.hidden=1
prop tag2 obj.name=tag2
prop tag2 beh.hidden=1
prop notice on.read=show|tag1\nshow|tag2
prop tally obj.name=tally
prop tally beh.use=Hand in the salvage tags
prop tally if.use=has|story:salvagetag|2\n!signal|tagsin
prop tally on.use=signal||tagsin\nshow|receipt\nmessage||The tally clerk's board takes two more marks. Next to it a receipt is waiting, already signed.
prop tally else.use=message||The tally board wants two salvage tags from the street below.
prop receipt on.read=signal||unionfriend

note charter Union charter | CHARTER OF THE SALVAGERS' UNION\n\nWhat we bring up, we share.\nNo diver goes down alone.\nNo diver is left down.\nThe Authority gets its tenth and not a nail more.\n\nThe hook is our sign. The rope is our oath.\n\n(Below, in chalk, the foreman's hand: Article five, never written, everyone knows it - when the Council's man comes with a form, you count the boots he's wearing and you remember he can't swim. - B.H.)\n\n(And below that, smaller: Article six. Whoever eats the last of the foreman's biscuits refills the tin. This means you, Carver. - B.H.)
note requisition Council requisition | HARBOR COUNCIL - REQUISITION No. 4412\n\nThe Salvagers' Union will deliver to the Council's barge, at the turn of each month:\n- all iron, steel and concrete raised from Lowstreet;\n- all engines, motors and pumps, whole or broken;\n- all stone.\n\nThese materials are needed for the Foundation works. Their tonnage is to be entered in the barge book and not in the Union's own tally.\n\nCompliance is a condition of the Union's licence.\n\n- Councillor Aldous Crane\n\n(Pencilled on the back: Why does he want stone? Nobody builds with stone any more. He's not building. He's sinking it. - B.)
note notice Missing expedition notice | MISSING - THE LOWSTREET EXPEDITION\n\nFive divers under Ines Marlowe went down to Lowstreet to map the old pumps. They have not come up.\n\nTheir salvage tags were found on the street below this jetty. Bring them up and hand them in at the tally.\n\nThe Union does not leave its divers down.\n\n(In the foreman's hand, under it: Ines would have my hide for putting her name first. She hated being in charge. She was only ever in charge because she was the one who asked the questions nobody else would. That was the expedition: questions. Who drowned Lowstreet's pumps, and why the Council paid for them to stay drowned. - B.H.)
note bramletter Bram's letter | On the hall floor, weighed down with a rivet -\n\nSo now you've read it. Eleven thousand tons, and I'm not a mad old man.\n\nI asked at Pumpcrown once where it all goes. Wilmer Dobbs - foreman at the Works, writes complaints the way other men breathe - said the Council's barges tie up at the Works first, every one, and sit low in the water, and leave lower. He said the pumps there make a noise at night like they're running the wrong way. He said a lot of things. Wilmer always does. But Wilmer is never wrong about pumps.\n\nThe Authority's waterworks answers on band nine hundred. You'll want an engine on that raft - you've got the plans from my desk. And if you meet Ines, tell her the Union is still keeping her hook on the wall.\n\n- Bram
note memorialsign Memorial wall | THE UNION REMEMBERS\n\nA hundred names, scratched into the concrete. The newest are only chalk: MARLOWE. OKONJO. FENN. THE TWO DALY BROTHERS.\n\nSomeone has drawn a small question mark next to MARLOWE, and someone else has rubbed it out, and the first someone has drawn it again, bigger.\n\nAt the bottom, cut deep: WHAT WE BRING UP, WE SHARE. WHO WE LOSE, WE KEEP.
note receipt Union receipt | RECEIVED: two salvage tags, Marlowe's team.\n\nThey were alive when they dropped them - the cords are cut, not torn. A diver cuts her tag off when she means to be thought dead.\n\nI'm not putting that in the tally. I'm putting it here, for you. If Ines is alive she had a reason to vanish, and the reason is on Lowstreet.\n\nThe Union owes you a diver's debt. - Bram Hask, foreman
note hallchest Hall desk | The hall's desk: the engine controls' plans, a foreman's whistle - and a spare diver's kit, an oxygen bottle and flippers. No diver goes down alone, and none goes down short of air.
note foremanbox Foreman's box | The yard foreman's box: the metal detector's plans, a list of what the street gave up this week.
note flarestore Flare store | The Union's flare store: the firework's plans, flares for divers in trouble.
note cranecab Crane cab | Crane three's cab: the zipline's plans, a thermos, a view over the yard.
note potatobox Planter box | Seed potatoes for the yard's planters.
note tag1 Salvage cache | A diver's cache on the street below, tied to a lamp post.
note tag2 Salvage cache | A diver's cache on the street below, wedged in a shop door.
loot hallchest Blueprint_EngineControls*1;MetalIngot*2;Bolt*4;OxygenBottle*1;Flipper*1
prop hallchest loot.refill=0
loot foremanbox Blueprint_MetalDetector*1;Scrap*4
prop foremanbox loot.refill=0
loot flarestore Blueprint_Firework*1;Rope*2
prop flarestore loot.refill=0
loot cranecab Blueprint_ZiplineBase*1;MetalIngot*2;Rope*3
prop cranecab loot.refill=0
loot potatobox Raw_Potato*4
prop potatobox loot.refill=0
loot tag1 story:salvagetag*1;Scrap*2
prop tag1 loot.refill=0
loot tag2 story:salvagetag*1;MetalOre*2
prop tag2 loot.refill=0

prop hallzone zone.id=union_hall
prop hallzone zone.radius=3
prop hallzone zone.message=The Union hall. Hooks on the walls, a board of names, and a desk nobody sits at.
prop crane3zone zone.id=crane_3
prop crane3zone zone.radius=4
prop crane3zone zone.message=Crane three. The zipline's end, and a cab up the ladder.
prop divezone zone.id=dive_rope
prop divezone zone.radius=3
prop divezone zone.message=The dive rope. Below it, in green water, the street lamps of Lowstreet.

note cranewreckcrate Toppled crane's toolbox | Crane five's toolbox. The crane came down in the last storm; the Union never had the parts to stand it up again.
loot cranewreckcrate Bolt*4;MetalIngot*2;Rope*2
note tallybook Tally book | UNION TALLY BOOK\n\nShare out: one part to the diver, one to the crane, one to the hall.\nThis week: a fridge, two doors, a tram seat. Lowstreet is picked nearly clean above the shops.\nMarlowe says the store at the east end is untouched. The Authority says it is closed. Why would a drowned shop be closed?\n\n(Carver's hand: A tram driver's cap came up today, off the depot steps on Lowstreet - JONAH PENN on the band, the man who drove the six-forty. Little Pip's dad, from the Rookery. I didn't have the heart to give it to her. Gave it to old Maud Penn instead. Unpaid share, one cap. Bram can dock my wages. - C.)\n\n(Bram's hand: Docked one biscuit. - B.)
note divercavechest Divers' locker | A diver's locker: a spare mask strap, rope and a tin of grease.
loot divercavechest Rope*3;Scrap*3;Leather*1
prop divercavechest loot.refill=0
